    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0420" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg350"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Campbell</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 26, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I send you herewith, for your information,
                    a memorandum<anchor n="*" xml:id="d239-f1"/> of a conversation which passed
                    between me and Mr. Berthemy, the minister of France to this country, on the 17th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>I have also to inform you that our consul at Vera Cruz, Mr. Lane, has resigned
                    his position, and that upon his recommendation the name of Mr. E. Saulnier, who
                    has on various occasions acted as consul of the United States to that city, has
                    been sent to the Senate for confirmation in his place.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis D. Campbell</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d239-f1" n="*" xml:id="d239-f1-content">
                <p>For this enclosure see correspondence with the French legation. Page 290, vol.
                    I.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
